# Projects

Full club projects live here. Each project gets its own folder.

## Structure

```
projects/
  <project-name>/
    README.md
    src/
```

## Active Projects

| Project | Lead | Status | Description |
|---|---|---|---|
| _None yet_ | | | Add yours via Pull Request |

## Starting a Project

1. Pick a short, lowercase, hyphenated name (e.g. `audit-sampler`)
2. Create `projects/<project-name>/README.md`
3. Add your code under `projects/<project-name>/src/`
4. Add a row to the table above
5. Open a Pull Request

## Project README Template

Copy this into your project's `README.md`:

```markdown
# Project Name

**Lead:** your GitHub username
**Status:** Idea / In Progress / Complete

## What It Does
One or two sentences.

## How to Run
Steps to install and run.

## Tools Used
Models, libraries, APIs.
```

Skills (small reusable tools) go in `skills/`, not here.
